// Alert 2 — a container-scoped ListBlobs: enumeration that is not a tenant prefix.
//
// Backs ARD-039 §5 (the download SAS carries no `list` permission) and KAT-417
// T-001's prefix invariant.
//
// Nothing in `app/` lists a container. Verified by grep at the time this was
// written: the product addresses every object by exact name, and the only call
// that looks like enumeration — `uncommitted_block_indexes` on the resume path —
// is `GetBlockList`, a different operation against a *single blob*, so it never
// appears here.
//
// The one legitimate enumeration is a **per-tenant prefix** listing, which is what
// a purge fix would use (`tenant_purge` leaves blobs today — docs/APP.md §30). Every
// blob name in this product begins with `{tenant_id}/` and `Tenant.id` is an
// integer, so a legitimate listing is `prefix=<digits>/` and anything else is
// either an operator with a portal open or someone walking the corpus.
//
// `parse_url` is how the requested prefix is recovered: ListBlobs puts it in the
// query string, not in a header or the path.
StorageBlobLogs
| where OperationName == "ListBlobs"
| where StatusCode >= 200 and StatusCode < 300
| extend RequestedPrefix = tostring(parse_url(Uri)["Query Parameters"]["prefix"])
// `not(x matches regex ...)`, not `x !matches regex ...` — KQL has no negated
// form of this operator, and the shorter spelling does not parse.
| where isempty(RequestedPrefix) or not(RequestedPrefix matches regex @"^[0-9]+/")
| project
    TimeGenerated,
    AccountName,
    RequestedPrefix,
    AuthenticationType,
    StatusCode,
    CallerIpAddress,
    UserAgentHeader,
    Uri
